  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CoCreateMyCity Kurdish Region of Iraq</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The series of five #CoCreateMyCity hackathons throughout the Kurdish Region of Iraq aim to set best practice examples for improved cooperation between the private sector and knowledge institutes. This will be done by using innovative and creative business solutions created by Iraqi student teams, as a practical means to solve challenges from the relevant local sector. On the one hand, participating students will experience a more entrepreneurial mindset and may be inspired to apply this mindset to other aspects of their lives. By means of the project, the private sector will become more attractive for participating students. On the other hand, the local private sector is provided with creative and innovative solutions for real challenges it faces. It also has the chance to get in touch with potential talent for their businesses, and can support knowledge institutes to better align with their needs. Lastly, knowledge institutes staff is given the chance to try-out a more hands on approach of teaching in which real challenges are solved in an innovative manner by their students.</narrative>
  </description>
